  "notes": ["Starts after original near-plane contact. The original actor carries a saved current support flag, allocated plane, and support owner. The host declares the same owner's previous/current root transforms but not the support identity.","The original startup prefix writes GQR5, captured before arena/OS initialization. The scoped carry replay uses that state for angle loads. The single zero-GQR row is an intentionally uninitialized harness control, not a retail behavior.","The original actor-update prefix reproduces the direct carry helper up to the next original call. Root translation follows the owner's frame and yaw adds the owner yaw delta modulo 16 bits. A joint-only translation does not move the root through this helper.","For the tested actor owner, a nonzero scene mask must include its seat bit; zero imposes no mask restriction. Inactive owners, non-one phases, and previous support alone all refuse carry.","The scope is the actor-owner path with declared zero pitch/roll and stance rotations. It does not execute a movement program, republish shapes, construct a moving platform, or qualify prop owners, hardware, or native gameplay."],
